(a) (a) The management of the establishment must take reasonable measures and precautions to ensure that all persons working in direct contact with animal food, animal food-contact surfaces, and animal food-packaging materials conform to hygienic practices to the extent necessary to protect against the contamination of animal food.
(b) (b) The methods for conforming to hygienic practices and maintaining cleanliness include:
(b)(1) (1) Maintaining adequate personal cleanliness;
